# --- editor / interpreter noise ---------------------------------------------
.claude*
*__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- output trees ------------------------------------------------------------
# These are NOT ignored wholesale any more. Each carries its own .gitignore that
# ignores its contents and re-includes only the small text that explains and
# reproduces a run:
#
#   biophysical-fusion/results/     per-run README.md, submit.sh, run scripts
#   biophysical-fusion/slurm_logs/  the archive-policy README + job manifests
#   mdcnn_eval/                     the MD-CNN reproduction's code and params
#   h1_repro/                       the leak-reproduction scripts
#   regulatory_msa/                 the promoter-MSA generators
#
# Numbers, figures, arrays, executed notebooks, saved models and raw job logs
# all stay untracked. Each of those .gitignore files is an ALLOWLIST (`*` then
# targeted `!` lines), so a new output format cannot leak in by default.
#
# Why this changed: results/experiments/alllocus_run/ — 221 jobs, ~350 GPU-hours
# — was deleted with no copy anywhere, because a blanket `results/` rule here
# meant its README and its findings lived in no repository at all. The write-up
# is what preserves a run; it belongs in git even when its outputs do not.
